cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EXOPHCA, cite it as below."
title: "EXOPHCA — Exoplanet Habitability Compatibility Analysis"
abstract: >-
  An educational data-science project that scores how closely known exoplanets
  and TESS Objects of Interest resemble Earth in radius and stellar insolation.
  It ships a Streamlit app whose every number is read from committed CSV files,
  and the reproducible pipeline that produced them: archive ingestion, Kopparapu
  habitable-zone classification, an ESI-style two-parameter similarity, a
  host-star-split radius model with conformal intervals, and explicit
  uncertainty propagation. Similarity is not habitability and none of it is
  evidence of life.
authors:
  - family-names: "Singh"
    given-names: "Gurjot"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gurjot-Singh-01/EXOPHCA"
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - habitable zone
  - earth similarity index
  - uncertainty propagation
  - streamlit
  - python
notes: >-
  Data snapshot: July 2026. The committed CSVs, the model artifact and every
  published metric belong to two NASA Exoplanet Archive exports retrieved that
  month. Regenerating from a later export will change the counts, the metrics
  and the artifact hash.
